  "body": "Raised by the contributor during #521's hands-on probe test on a real Tormach 770MX, 2026-11-09 (\"should we explicitly set S0? speed to 0 for probes\").\n\n**Today:** since #523 (PR #526) a probe op posts no spindle start (no `S0 M3`, no `M3`), and the program's only `M5` is at its end. The probe is safe on the 770MX because PathPilot's `M6` stops the spindle during the tool change. That is a property of the control, though, not something the program says. A control or post path whose tool change does not stop the spindle (a manual tool change, a same-tool continuation, a dialect whose `M6` leaves `M3` modal) would bring a probe to the part with the previous op's spindle still turning.\n\n**Expected:** every post writes an explicit `M5` after a probe's tool change and length offset, before its first move: `T99 M6` / `G43 H99` / `M5`. This is defensive and idempotent. The word is `M5`, not `S0`: `S0` only sets a speed value, and some controls ignore it or refuse it.\n\n**Done means:** each shipped post (tormach, haas, fanuc, sinumerik, mazak, heidenhain) emits its spindle-stop word between the probe's tool change and its first motion. A test (alongside `probe_spindle`) pins the order per dialect, and a cutting op's output is unchanged.\n\nRelated: #523, #521, #570.\n",
